From 4fe54fc4a91c2f662fc044da1e23a1ea64ae4cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Lopez Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 11:32:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 019/130] watchdog: sunxi_wdt: restart priority 200 to beat
 PSCI (reboot hung on T527)

The SYSTEM_RESET of the ATF/BL31 of the BSP does not reset: the PSCI call
gets stuck without returning. With the driver standard priority (128) the
PSCI handler (129) runs first -> 'reboot' froze the board forever (not even
with SUNXI_WATCHDOG=y did it work; the user always had to cut power).
Priority 200 makes the reset go through the watchdog, like the BSP 5.15.
Local workaround for the BSP firmware; revisit if it moves to mainline ATF.
---
 drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
index b6c761acc..ce209563c 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -282,7 +282,14 @@ static int sunxi_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	watchdog_init_timeout(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, timeout, dev);
 	watchdog_set_nowayout(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, nowayout);
-	watchdog_set_restart_priority(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, 128);
+	/*
+	 * Priority > 129 (the PSCI handler): on the T527/OPi4A the
+	 * SYSTEM_RESET of the ATF BSP hangs without returning, and with
+	 * the standard priority (128 < 129) this handler never got to
+	 * run -> `reboot` froze the board. The BSP 5.15 also resets via
+	 * watchdog. Revisit if it ever moves to mainline ATF.
+	 */
+	watchdog_set_restart_priority(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, 200);
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, sunxi_wdt);
 
